  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Thinly slice the cabbage with a sharp knife or mandoline. Thinly slice the spring onion, keeping the white and green parts separate. Cut the tomato into 1cm chunks. Crush or finely chop 2 garlic cloves.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2712496/photos/large/prep_ingredients-e4441d7a4bf1f8eddc1b974a3b15f4ff.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir-fry cabbage: Melt 10g butter and 2 tsp vegetable oil in a medium deep frypan over medium-high heat. Stir-fry the cabbage for 2-3 mins until just tender (see Kitchen 101). Season with salt and pepper, then remove from the pan.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2712497/photos/large/stir_fry_cabbage-ecbb9f64efa45fead25deb51518eabe5.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Brown plant-based mince: Heat 2 tsp vegetable oil in the same pan over medium-high heat. Cook the plant-based mince, breaking up the lumps with a spoon, for 5-6 mins until browned. Increase the heat to high and add the masala seasoning, garlic and white part of the spring onion, then stir-fry for 1 min or until fragrant.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2712498/photos/large/brown_lamb_mince-bec3a0f06785cae62321508116ff805f.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Finish stir-fry: Add the cabbage to the mince mixture and stir-fry for 1-2 mins until warmed through. Taste, then season with salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2712499/photos/large/finish_stir_fry-cff3f65a9bdc80a5fd17c8a35dd0f578.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Divide the stir-fry among bowls, scatter over the tomato and remaining spring onion. Drizzle with the yoghurt and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2712500/photos/large/serve_up-9ca902488d5b0491d0c420f6127c519e.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen 101: Fast and hot is key when stir-frying! Make sure you cook over the heat indicated, stirring constantly so everything is cooked evenly. We've used a deep frypan, but you can use a wok if you have one.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2712501/photos/large/kitchen_101-97c9c3f914c0e3bf94ae6422fbfeb553.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
